  "name": "An Orchid Room",
  "description": "One of the private rooms upstairs at the Glass Orchid: plum walls with a woven orchid pattern, dark lacquer and gold lattice. A wide low bed in black and plum silk under a long window, its sheer curtain half drawn on Velvet's pink neon. A dressing table with a ring of mirror bulbs, perfume bottles and a glass orchid, beside a gold-painted lacquer screen with a silk robe over it. Two velvet armchairs and tea for two under a pink orchid-bud lamp. Paper lanterns on either side of the bed. By the door, a brass call panel with a red light; high in the corner, a camera dome with a green pinpoint. Everything is the house's.",
